## 7. Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)

To absorb unexpected viral traffic spikes of **1M+ concurrent users**, deploy this Horizontal Pod Autoscaler manifest. It scales pods from **3 up to 30 replicas** based on CPU and memory thresholds:

```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: kaiprakriti-backend
  namespace: production
  labels:
    app: kaiprakriti-backend
spec:
  replicas: 4
  strategy:
    rollingUpdate:
      maxSurge: 25%
      maxUnavailable: 0
    type: RollingUpdate
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: kaiprakriti-backend
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: kaiprakriti-backend
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: app
        image: kaiprakriti/backend:v2.0
        ports:
        - containerPort: 3000
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: "500m"
            memory: "512Mi"
          limits:
            cpu: "2000m"
            memory: "2048Mi"
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /health/live
            port: 3000
          initialDelaySeconds: 10
          periodSeconds: 15
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /health/ready
            port: 3000
          initialDelaySeconds: 5
          periodSeconds: 10
---
apiVersion: autoscaling/v2
kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler
metadata:
  name: kaiprakriti-hpa
  namespace: production
spec:
  scaleTargetRef:
    apiVersion: apps/v1
    kind: Deployment
    name: kaiprakriti-backend
  minReplicas: 3
  maxReplicas: 30
  metrics:
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: cpu
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 65
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: memory
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 75
